Voxel PALETTE-BLEND TILE builder (extender FUN_0000_bc9c) -- restore ac70's dropped index return so
the 256x256 pairwise-blend LUT (tile DAT_0000_3918) is filled with real nearest-palette indices.

DEFINITIVE PRODUCER (docs/oracle_tile3918_producer.md, CR3-aware fixed-phys oracle capture):
tile 3918 is a 256x256 pairwise PALETTE-BLEND LUT built at MAP-LOAD by bc9c:
    tile[cl + 256*ch] = tile[ch + 256*cl] = ac70( (pal[cl] + pal[ch]) / 2 )
where pal = the 256-entry 6-bit VGA MISSION palette at ext ds:0x5598 and ac70 = the nearest-palette
reverse-lookup (patch 288's a060/a460/a860 + 0x4f60, verified working -> 85b8 = 112 distinct desert).

ASM (re_out/fist_image.bin 0xbc9c..0xbd0d), the write of the blended index:
    bceb: call 0xac70            ; ac70 returns the nearest palette index in BL
    bcf2: mov  [ecx],bl          ; tile[ch*256+cl] = index
    bcf4: xchg ch,cl
    bcf6: mov  [ecx],bl          ; tile[cl*256+ch] = index  (symmetric mirror)

BUG (flat32 decompile, dropped __allregs multi-register return -- same class patch 236 fixed for
9e60): the pristine bc9c body reads
    bVar12 = bVar11;             ; bVar11 = pal[cl].R (a blend input, NOT the result)
    FUN_0000_ac70();             ; return VALUE dropped
    *pbVar8 = bVar12;            ; writes pal[cl].R over the tile
so the tile filled with palette RED bytes (55 distinct) instead of blended indices, AND the renderer
9200 (which SMC-samples ds:0x3918) saw an empty/wrong tile -> black terrain.  The blend triple
ac68/ac69/ac6a and the symmetric CONCAT pointer math are already faithful (verified vs asm; the base
ds:0xbc90 low-16 = 0 so cl/ch index the 64 KB dest correctly); ONLY the write source was wrong.

FIX: consume ac70's return (already typed `undefined4` by patch 236) as the blended index and write it
to both symmetric slots -- exactly asm `bl = ac70(); [ecx]=bl; xchg; [ecx]=bl`.

EFFECT: with [ds:0xbc90] pointed at the tile buffer at build time (the shim's "bc90 REUSED = tile"
alias, tools/native_main.c op-0x18), tile 3918 goes from EMPTY (distinct=1) to distinct=175/176 with
real blended indices (was writing palette-red bytes = 55 distinct).  Class: dropped multi-register
__allregs return.

HONEST STATUS (measured vs scratch/oracle/oracle_tile3918.bin, verified stable == phys 0x175200 in
four RAM dumps): this is NOT yet byte-exact (best 32.6% identical at window=0).  The oracle tile is
NON-symmetric (15.7% symmetric in the pure bc9c region) whereas bc9c writes a SYMMETRIC pairwise LUT --
so the doc's "symmetric pairwise palette-blend" model does NOT alone reproduce the observed tile, and
the window/low-16-offset reconciliation (bc9c fills 0x40000-aligned, tile windows at 0x4200) is also
disproven (0x4200 -> 1.1% match).  ROOT CAUSE, oracle-proven: the tile is built from a BUILD-TIME
DISPLAY palette 4f60 the port does not reproduce -- oracle build-time 4f60 has system colours (white at
index 63) in the reserved 0..79 range and ac64<63, while the port's a033 builds 4f60 = mission_pal>>1
(only 0..23 nonzero) and reads the dump-time reserved-count 80.  The true frontier is UPSTREAM: the
display-palette construction + reserved-count/ac64 handling at map-load.  Patch 289 remains a correct,
asm-verified fix (the dropped ac70 return is unambiguously a bug); it is a prerequisite, not the whole
producer.  Mission-path only (op 0x18 / bc9c) -> the 19 menu verify flows are byte-untouched.

